# DocAtlas core rules

This project uses DocAtlas (https://github.com/JeeEko/DocAtlas) for documentation.

## Before making changes

1. Read `doc-atlas/docs/AI_CONTEXT.md` if it exists (compact orientation)
2. Read `AGENTS.md` and `doc-atlas/docs/START_HERE.md`
3. Check `doc-atlas/docs/` for architecture, onboarding, and runbook context
4. If behavior changes, plan doc updates in the same change

## Architecture-sensitive work

For changes involving APIs, contracts, events, databases, integrations, infrastructure, auth, deployment, or business flows:

1. Read `doc-atlas/docs/AI_CONTEXT.md` and relevant context/journey docs
2. Treat source code as authoritative if docs conflict
3. After material changes, invoke or recommend **`docatlas-skill-update`** before finishing

## Documentation standards

- Write in plain English for developers new to this repo
- Use confidence tags: `[verified]`, `[likely]`, `[uncertain]`, `[planned]`
- Use epistemic labels: OBSERVED, DECLARED, INFERRED, UNKNOWN
- Cite evidence paths: `src/file.ts#L10`
- Do not mark content `[verified]` unless confirmed against code or tests
- Replace `TODO` and `TBD` placeholders when you fill in content

## Drift prevention

- Run `docatlas drift` after doc changes
- Update `doc-atlas/docs/GLOSSARY.md` when introducing new domain terms
- Keep `doc-atlas/docs/RUNBOOK.md` commands copy-paste accurate

## Do not

- Invent features not in the codebase
- Skip doc updates for user-facing behavior changes
- Delete existing documentation without team reason
- Promote INFERRED or UNKNOWN claims to OBSERVED without evidence
